---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'How it works — Noven';
const description =
  'How Noven gets your business found by AI assistants: a £30 audit of where you stand, a one-off Foundation setup, and an ongoing monthly plan to keep you visible.';

const howToSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'AI assistant visibility for service businesses',
  serviceType: 'Business visibility in AI assistant recommendations',
  provider: { '@id': new URL('/#organization', Astro.site).href },
  areaServed: 'GB',
  description:
    'Noven audits how AI assistants such as ChatGPT, Google, Copilot and Perplexity currently answer questions about a business, fixes what is blocking the business from being found, and maintains that visibility month to month.',
};
---

<Base title={title} description={description} schema={[howToSchema]}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>How does Noven get you found?</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Three stages, in order: find out where you stand, fix what's in the way, then keep you
        visible as the AI systems change. Each stage only makes sense if the previous one says
        it's worth doing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>The audit — £30, one-off</h3>
            <p>
              We start by asking the major AI assistants the questions your customers would ask —
              in your service area, in your specialism — and recording exactly what they say. We
              check whether they know your business exists, what they believe about you, whether
              it's accurate, and who they recommend instead of you.
            </p>
            <p>
              Then we look at why. We check what the AI crawlers can and can't read on your
              website, whether the basic facts about your business are consistent across the
              places these systems draw from, and whether anything on your site answers the
              questions being asked.
            </p>
            <p>
              You get a short written report in plain English: where you show up today, what's
              blocking you, and what we'd do about it. If you're already in good shape, the report
              says so and we don't try to sell you the next stage.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>The Foundation — £350, one-off</h3>
            <p>
              This is the setup work that makes your business readable and credible to AI
              systems. Working on your existing website — we don't rebuild websites — the
              Foundation typically covers:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Making sure AI crawlers are allowed in and can read your pages as plain text, not
                just as a rendered app.
              </li>
              <li>
                Adding structured data: machine-readable statements of who you are, what you do,
                where you operate and what you charge, in the format these systems are built to
                consume.
              </li>
              <li>
                Getting the basic facts about your business — name, services, location, contact
                details — consistent everywhere they appear online.
              </li>
              <li>
                Writing or restructuring key pages so they directly answer the questions your
                customers ask, in language an assistant can quote.
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              The exact scope comes from your audit, so you're never paying for work you don't
              need.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Ongoing — from £75 a month</h3>
            <p>
              AI assistants re-crawl, re-rank and change their sources continually, so visibility
              is something you maintain, not something you buy once. The monthly plans exist at
              three levels of effort: <strong>Maintain</strong> keeps what the Foundation built
              current and checks how you're showing up; <strong>Grow</strong> adds new
              answer-focused content each month so you appear for more of your customers'
              questions; <strong>Lead</strong> is for businesses that want to be the default
              recommendation in their field. Details are on the
              <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>What don't we do?</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          <strong>We don't guarantee recommendations.</strong> Nobody controls what an AI
          assistant says, and anyone promising you a guaranteed spot in its answers is guessing
          or lying. What we do is make sure everything these systems demonstrably rely on is in
          place for your business — and show you, in plain before-and-after terms, how you're
          showing up.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>We don't build websites.</strong> The work happens on the site you already
          have. If your site has problems beyond our scope, the audit will say so honestly.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>We don't do lock-ins.</strong> The audit and Foundation are one-off payments.
          Monthly plans roll month to month. [PLACEHOLDER: confirm cancellation notice period.]
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Ready to find out where you stand?</h2>
      <p>
        The audit costs £30 and tells you exactly where you appear today — including the awkward
        finding that you might not need us.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Book the £30 audit</a>
        <a href="/pricing/">See full pricing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
